\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 The Exercise Regression Hierarchy\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 To operationalize load management and biopsychosocial principles, coaches require a structured algorithm to modify exercises when an athlete reports pain. When an athlete asks, "My shoulder hurts on the press\'97what do I do?" or "Can I train through this?", the coach must avoid the extremes of telling the athlete to completely stop training or to mindlessly push through severe pain. Instead, the coach applies an Exercise Regression Hierarchy, systematically modifying variables until a pain-tolerable entry point is found.\
The goal is to maintain the highest possible training effect while keeping symptoms at an acceptable level (typically defined as a pain score of 3-4 out of 10 that subsides rapidly after the session and does not cause elevated pain the following morning). The regression hierarchy modifies variables in the following order:\

