\f0\b \cf2 5. Movement Vector
\f1\b0 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 If the primary movement vector is entirely intolerable, change the angle of the push or pull. This shifts the stress to different synergistic muscle groups while keeping the athlete active.\cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Switch from an overhead press (vertical) to an incline press or landmine press (diagonal).\cell \lastrow\row
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Through this hierarchy, the coach ensures the athlete continues to train, thereby preventing disuse syndrome, managing the ACWR, and breaking the fear-avoidance cycle.\
