\f0\b\fs48 \cf2 Algorithmic Hypertrophy: A Sports-Science Knowledge Base Architecture for AI Coaching Systems\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf2 Executive Overview of the Algorithmic Architecture\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 The translation of physiological resistance training adaptations into deterministic, computational models requires a highly structured knowledge base. The following architectural report outlines the foundational logic required to encode muscular hypertrophy parameters into an artificial intelligence coaching system. By synthesizing current meta-analytical dose-response regressions, neuromuscular fatigue kinetics, and psychophysiological strain markers, this framework constructs a parameterized logic engine. The system shifts training prescriptions from static, heuristic-based templates to dynamic algorithms that adjust volume, proximity to failure, and load magnitude based on real-time biofeedback.\
To satisfy the data structuring requirements of an AI logic engine, the biological mechanisms have been categorized into discrete modules, evidence records, and topic abstractions. The primary module, designated as 
\fs30 \cf5 \cb6 \strokec5 hypertrophy
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  (Muscle Hypertrophy), acts as the central governing node for all structural adaptations, dictating phase routing during caloric deficits ("cut"), maintenance ("maintain"), and surpluses ("gain"). The overarching logic mandates that hypertrophy is primarily mediated by mechanical tension and metabolic stress, which the system must titrate carefully against the athlete's recovery capacity and psychophysiological strain.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

