\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Parameter 1: Volume Landmarks (MEV, MRV, and MED)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 The most robust predictor of muscular hypertrophy is the dose-response relationship of weekly set volume. Resistance training volume\'97defined algorithmically as the number of hard sets performed per muscle group per week\'97demonstrates a graded, positive correlation with increases in muscle cross-sectional area.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 The Dose-Response Curve and Baseline Assignments\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 The data indicates that each additional weekly set is associated with an increase in effect size of 0.023, corresponding to a 0.37% increase in the percentage of muscle mass gained. This continuous variable necessitates that the AI coaching system establishes a Minimum Effective Volume (MEV) and a Maximum Recoverable Volume (MRV) for each user. For the vast majority of trained men and women, the optimal operational bandwidth lies between 12 and 20 weekly sets per muscle group.\
The system logic must assign baseline volumes dynamically based on the user's training age. Novice trainees achieve maximal stimulation at lower volumes, whereas resistance-trained individuals require higher thresholds to disrupt homeostasis. In controlled trials, trained men performing five sets per exercise per session achieved significantly greater hypertrophy in the elbow flexors and lateral thighs compared to those performing one or three sets. Therefore, the AI initializes advanced users closer to the 12-15 set threshold.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 Aging and Volume Non-Responsiveness\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 Chronological age functions as an independent modifier in the volume algorithm. Older adults often display an element of anabolic resistance, rendering them non-responsive to lower training volumes. Evidence suggests that increasing weekly training volume is necessary to overcome this non-responsiveness, allowing older populations to achieve muscle growth rates comparable to younger cohorts. Consequently, the system applies a positive volume multiplier to user profiles over the age of fifty, elevating their Minimum Effective Dose (MED) to ensure sufficient mechanical tension is applied to trigger mammalian target of rapamycin (mTOR) signaling pathways.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 Parameter 2: Fractional Quantification and Exercise Selection\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 A critical failure point in legacy coaching models is the rudimentary counting of sets on a 1:1 basis, regardless of the exercise's biomechanical complexity. To prevent systemic overreaching, the AI implements fractional quantification for all indirect sets.\
Multi-level meta-regressions reveal that volume and frequency exhibit unique dose-response relationships when sets are categorized as direct or indirect. The posterior probability of the marginal slope exceeding zero for the effect of volume on hypertrophy is 100%, but the predictive validity of this model requires indirect sets to be fractionally quantified.\

